155	    /**
156	     * the correct way to get a local is to call createCompilerLocal,
157	     * which will give you a stack offset that acts as a handle on the
158	     * local variable you requested, and then to hand that local
159	     * variable back again when you're done by calling
160	     * disposeCompilerLocal so that debug information can be generated
161	     * where possible, and so that stack slots can be reused in a
162	     * sensible way.  If you are representing a variable in Fortress
163	     * source code, you should do this in the constructor for a
164	     * VarCodeGen; CodeGen maintains a lexEnv that maps a Fortress
165	     * variable to the corresponding VarCodeGen. */
166	
167	    // Non-user-accessible local variable
168	    public int createCompilerLocal(String _name, String type) {
169	        if (localVariableCount != varNames.size()) {
170	            throw new CompilerError("Trying to create local " + _name +
171	                                       " but current metadata is off\nlocalVariableCount = " +
172	                                       localVariableCount +
173	                                       "\nvarNames = " + varNames);
174	        }
175	        Debug.debug(Debug.Type.CODEGEN, 2,
176	                    "LOCAL create ", localVariableCount, " ", _name);
177	        varNames.add(_name);
178	        varTypes.add(type);
179	        Label start = new Label();
180	        visitLabel(start);
181	        varFirstUse.add(start);
182	
183	        return localVariableCount++;
184	    }
